WHO HOLDS WHAT

This repository is a fork of PuzzleScript Next. Its parts have different
copyright holders. All of them are offered under the MIT terms below, except
the material listed under "Not covered".

- The map and sprite editor (puzzlescript-map-editor/) and the tooling this
  fork provides (tools/, doc/, the front page index.html, runserver.sh and
  runserver.bat, and .github/workflows/):
  Copyright (c) 2026 fortress-rhythm.
  puzzlescript-map-editor/ also carries its own LICENSE file.

- Everything else, meaning the engine, its editor and its documentation, and
  this fork's changes to them:
  Copyright (c) 2013 Stephen Lavelle, and the contributors to PuzzleScript,
  PuzzleScript Plus, Pattern:Script and PuzzleScript Next.

SCOPE

The MIT license below does not cover the third-party games and other
third-party material stored here.

Not covered:

- Example games by other authors: src/demo/, the copies of games in
  src/tests/resources/, and puzzlescript-map-editor/fixtures/games/.
- Gallery images and listings: src/Gallery/ and src/games_dat*.js.

These belong to their authors. They came with the upstream repository and their
license terms have not been confirmed. Upstream's src/demo/README says: "These
demos aren't necessarily under MIT license." Check with the author before reusing
one. See "Example games and licensing" in README.md.

Bundled fonts and libraries keep their own licenses. See credits/ and the notices
in those files.

Palettes in palettes/ that come from other artists are credited in each file, and
this fork does not relicense them.

